# Declarative SSH client configuration — owned by the guixcfg ssh
# application. Rebuilt from the Home generation on every boot; edit
# the repository, not this file.
#
# known_hosts persistence: SSH's atomic rewrite (mkstemp + rename) is
# incompatible with single-file bind mounts and with symlinks (rename
# replaces the symlink itself), so the mutable TOFU state lives at its
# canonical backing path and SSH is pointed at it via direct reference
# (docs/architecture/persistence.md) — the same pattern as the system
# sshd HostKey (/persist/system/ssh). The backing directory is created
# by the ssh application's system activation (root, owned by the user).
#
# Host-specific blocks must precede the generic `Host *` block:
# OpenSSH uses the first obtained value per parameter.

Host aur.archlinux.org
    IdentityFile ~/.ssh/aur
    User aur

Host *
    IdentityFile ~/.ssh/id_ed25519
    IdentitiesOnly yes
    UserKnownHostsFile /persist/data-app/ssh/known_hosts
    HashKnownHosts yes
